From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:48:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] msm-firmware-loader: link the blobs in image/ subfolders too

The SM4450 boards keep their WPSS in the modem partition's image/adrastea/, which the loader never linked, so it came from /lib/firmware. Link the files of each image/ subfolder after every top-level blob, so a top-level name still wins and the .mdt alias below covers them.
---
 msm-firmware-loader.sh | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/msm-firmware-loader.sh b/msm-firmware-loader.sh
index dfbe0fc..da3944e 100644
--- a/msm-firmware-loader.sh
+++ b/msm-firmware-loader.sh
@@ -290,6 +290,14 @@ do
 	ln -s "$dir"/* "$BASEDIR/blobs/" 2>/dev/null || :
 done
 
+# Some modem images keep a subsystem in a subfolder of image/: the SM4450
+# boards' WPSS is image/adrastea/wpss.mdt. Link those files too, after every
+# top-level blob, so a top-level name still wins.
+for dir in "$BASEDIR"/mnt/*/image/*/
+do
+	ln -s "$dir"* "$BASEDIR/blobs/" 2>/dev/null || :
+done
+
 # Some kernel versions expect .mbn instead of legacy .mdt
 # Symlink these files together, the kernel can autodetect the type.
 for mdt in "$BASEDIR"/blobs/*.mdt
